WEBVTT

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:30.540
Space Era

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:30.540
Imperial Year

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:01.190
What ?

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.860
That damned brat's going to
inherit the Lohengramm Countship ?

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.800
Is that true,
Secretary of State ?

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.750
He will soon be
twenty years old.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:13.190
For rendering distinguished
service in this battle...

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:16.250
...it's certain that he'll
be promoted to High Admiral...

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:20.540
...showing His Majesty's desire
to wish him well, as an adult.

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:22.640
Isn't the Lohengramm Countship...

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:25.590
...a famous family from the
founding of the Galactic Empire ?

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:31.490
Now that the direct line is extinct,
there are many nobles worthy of that title.

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:34.520
And you're going to give
that to that upstart ?

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:36.800
This is the will of
His Majesty the Kaiser.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:40.540
His Majesty is a
troublesome person, too.

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:47.390
Having just given the title of Countess Grunewald to a poor noble's girl...

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:50.640
...he'll now elevate her
little brother to Count ?

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:54.200
What Your Excellency the Prince
is saying goes too far.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:10.690
We managed to
come home safely.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:13.730
Yeah.
To your beloved wife ?

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:14.400
Yeah.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:17.940
This is thanks
to him, too...?

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:19.140
Yes.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:22.810
But it seems we'll be able to manage
pretty comfortably under him.

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:24.780
What ?
Are you dissatisfied ?

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:27.750
No.
It's quite desirable.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:30.740
But how far can he go,
beating his wings...?

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:38.000
Are you at a loss due to 
Prince Braunschweig's controlling ways ?

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:41.650
But by marrying
His Majesty's daughter...

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:45.770
...he probably thinks
he has property rights.

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:50.140
But this time, isn't there
some truth in what he says ?

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.680
Yes.
About that brat.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.780
Certainly, His Majesty's patronage
is also being called into question.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:59.890
But that brat cannot
be dismissed altogether.

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:04.720
This time, the Space Fleet Commander in Chief also recognizes his distinguished services.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:07.350
Fleet Admiral Muckenberger ?!

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:10.690
His Majesty the Kaiser
may also be impressed.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.600
Maybe so.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:17.300
If his political influence on the Imperial Household
increases more than this I won't be able to ignore it.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:21.140
If there's a bad bud,
I want to snip it quickly.

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:22.250
Like so...

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:36.440
No need to guide me.
The Countess is here, right ?

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:40.700
I'm fine, do
whatever you like.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:41.740
Baroness ?

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:49.100
Here, after all ?

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:52.720
This is a pretty sudden
visit, isn't it, Baroness ?

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:02.090
No, I got some
very good news...

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:04.990
...so I thought I'd hurry
over and let you know.

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:07.760
Your little brother won !

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.770
They say they'll
arrive on Odin today !

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:14.090
But they're saying some nonsense
about it being a military secret...

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:16.760
...so they couldn't announce it
publicly until just beforehand.

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:21.050
Reinhard...Sieg...

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:51.440
Your Excellency,
we've arrived.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:53.140
Yes, thank you.

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:54.140
Sir !

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:02.550
Let's go, Kircheis, and inform
my sister of our victory.

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:05.120
Yes, Lord Reinhard.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:16.040
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:16.040
<b>OF THE</b>

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:16.040
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:24.940
<b>Overture to a New Battle</b>

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:29.590
Hurrah for the
Imperial Fleet !

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:32.720
Hurrah for His
Excellency von Musel !

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:36.620
Hurrah for the
Imperial Fleet !

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:38.680
Hurrah for His
Excellency von Musel !

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:49.660
Your way of fighting was splendid.
I'm quite satisfied.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:54.350
Hereafter, I want to make the
most of your talents and abilities...

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:55.350
...for my sake.

00:05:58.350 --> 00:05:59.570
As you will !

00:05:58.650 --> 00:05:59.570
As you will !

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:05.250
Yang !

00:07:17.890 --> 00:07:20.350
Good work,
Your Excellency, Yang !

00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:26.250
Cut it out, Lap.

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:29.090
Sorry...

00:07:29.090 --> 00:07:31.690
But didn't you stand
out this time, too ?

00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:33.590
Next time it'll be "Your Excellency
the Rear Admiral," right ?

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:35.690
Because, at the same time, 
you're reluctant to advance, right ?

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:38.200
I probably won't be
promoted this time.

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:41.640
However, maybe Attenborough
will be promoted.

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:44.690
Oh, dear. To be
outstripped by my junior...

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:46.580
No...
Not by me...

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:51.570
Lap, if you hadn't
been sick, by now you'd...

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:53.490
No, forget it.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:55.590
I can't advance like Yang.

00:07:55.590 --> 00:07:59.090
By the way, it seems
Jessica was here too, but...

00:07:59.090 --> 00:08:00.990
She's waiting outside.

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:05.600
Before you see her, there's a little 
something the two of us have to talk about.

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:10.760
Then, with this, I'll...

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:12.240
Oh, really ? Sorry.

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:13.350
I'll see you again later.

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:14.820
Yeah.  Bye.

00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:18.700
So, what is this "talk ?"

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:22.830
Let's sit down.

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:30.750
Say, Yang...

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:33.200
...how many years have
we known each other ?

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:36.640
Twelve years ?

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:37.940
Yeah.

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:43.090
Well, you see, thinking that I'd
like to come to a conclusion soon...

00:08:43.090 --> 00:08:45.740
...I was waiting until you returned.

00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:47.090
Conclusion ?

00:08:47.090 --> 00:08:48.140
Yeah.

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:50.740
I'm thinking of
marrying Jessica.

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:57.350
Is it alright ?

00:08:57.350 --> 00:08:58.550
Why ?

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:00.700
It's strange.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:01.640
What is ?

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:02.670
Well...

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:04.540
...asking you.

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:06.730
Isn't it OK ?

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:08.640
Is it really alright ?

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:09.670
Yeah.

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:11.040
Be happy.

00:09:11.990 --> 00:09:15.240
Jessica hasn't
even said OK yet.

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:16.790
She will.

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:18.750
Will she...?

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:20.700
She will.

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:24.670
What's the matter ?
Get a hold of yourself  !

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:25.700
Y...yeah...

00:09:31.350 --> 00:09:32.660
Thanks, Yang.

00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:42.600
I will give directions to everyone 
who is waiting to greet someone.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:50.430
Just now, at Gate #59,
the 2nd Fleet is arriving...

00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:30.650
Jean Robert, get a
hold of yourself.

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:32.610
It can't be helped.

00:13:32.610 --> 00:13:34.610
He makes me worry
about our future.

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:42.810
Jessica, can you
get him home ?

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:44.540
Yeah.

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:50.660
Say, Yang...

00:13:51.580 --> 00:13:53.640
This guy's a good one.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:55.700
Jessica, you can be happy.

00:13:55.700 --> 00:13:57.650
Yes, I know.

00:14:17.610 --> 00:14:19.770
Sorry, Yang...

00:14:21.430 --> 00:14:22.590
Thanks.

00:15:19.670 --> 00:15:21.700
This carriage
is so slow  !

00:15:21.700 --> 00:15:24.550
You've been saying that quite a
bit since a little while ago, eh ?

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:27.550
I can't help it,
because it's the truth !

00:15:28.050 --> 00:15:30.740
In the first place,
this palace is too big !

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:33.900
And to make people use
Renaissance-style horse carriages here...

00:15:33.900 --> 00:15:35.750
...is both irrational and gaudy !

00:15:36.630 --> 00:15:43.500
You won't forgive anything that makes
you late to see Lady Annerose, will you ?

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:46.890
You're talking as
if you understand.

00:15:46.890 --> 00:15:48.590
Yes, I understand.

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:50.620
Because I feel
the same way.

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:52.300
You...

00:16:13.440 --> 00:16:14.440
Up !

00:16:19.730 --> 00:16:20.740
Oh, dear...

00:16:20.740 --> 00:16:25.200
An Imperial Admiral, of all people,
doing handstands on the lawn...?

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:28.650
It feels good
to defy gravity  !

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:35.560
Sister !

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:47.090
Although you two have grown
up and succeeded in life...

00:16:47.090 --> 00:16:50.140
...in some ways you haven't changed a bit since childhood, have you.

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:52.730
I have changed.
Regrettably.

00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:56.660
Oh, really ?
In what way, Reinhard ?

00:16:56.660 --> 00:17:00.300
I can stand on my hands
a lot longer than I used to.

00:17:00.300 --> 00:17:01.440
Oh, my !

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:19.670
Hi, Julian.
Good morning.

00:17:19.670 --> 00:17:22.090
Good morning,
Rear Admiral Cazellnu.

00:17:22.090 --> 00:17:24.990
Your guardian is sleeping
in as usual, isn't he ?

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:27.760
Yes !  Because he came
home drunk late last night.

00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:29.140
Really ?

00:17:29.140 --> 00:17:32.090
Then he's hung over
and passed out ?

00:17:32.090 --> 00:17:33.900
Ask him to call me
when he gets up.

00:17:35.090 --> 00:17:36.240
Roger !

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:39.740
Commodore !

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:41.600
Please get up !

00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:42.700
I've made
you breakfast.

00:17:45.590 --> 00:17:48.580
I'm not hungry...
And my head hurts...

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:51.590
Hung over, huh ?

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:54.600
It's rare for you to drink too
much outside the house, isn't it ?

00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:56.690
Did something happen ?

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:01.050
Lap and Jessica
are getting married.

00:18:04.090 --> 00:18:05.090
Drinking in celebration ?

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:08.700
Well, yeah...
So let me sleep...

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:11.740
And I just got back
from the front lines.

00:18:11.740 --> 00:18:14.680
Nobody's going to 
object if I celebrate.

00:18:14.680 --> 00:18:16.200
Understood.

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:18.760
But Rear Admiral Cazellnu
said to please call him.

00:18:19.730 --> 00:18:20.800
I've told you.

00:18:21.980 --> 00:18:23.560
Yeah, yeah.

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:31.690
Drinking in desperation...?

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:39.590
Although it's good to render 
distinguished services...

00:18:39.590 --> 00:18:42.760
...share them a little
with other people.

00:18:44.610 --> 00:18:48.540
Nobody can hold everything
in their hands.

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:49.680
Yes, I know.

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:53.620
Although I really
wish it were so.

00:18:57.690 --> 00:18:59.830
Don't worry, Lady Annerose.

00:18:59.830 --> 00:19:02.090
According to the
orders so far...

00:19:02.090 --> 00:19:05.600
...Lord Reinhard probably won't have to go to the front lines for a while.

00:19:06.570 --> 00:19:09.340
If so, maybe I'm
a little relieved.

00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:14.430
Admiral von Musel, inheriting
the Lohengramm Countship...

00:19:14.430 --> 00:19:18.620
...as well as being promoted to High Admiral, will lead an expeditionary force...

00:19:18.620 --> 00:19:23.760
...invading Free Planets Alliance
territory to subjugate the rebels.

00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:27.760
To test if he has the actual
power suitable to the rank ?

00:19:27.760 --> 00:19:33.570
If he doesn't, I won't be able to
quiet the high nobles' grumbling.

00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:36.590
But does he have
such talent...?

00:19:36.590 --> 00:19:40.990
If not, then he doesn't; and if he dies in battle, then His Majesty will also give up.

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:45.670
But if he does, I also think there's
value in taking advantage of that.

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:48.790
For you, too.

00:19:49.570 --> 00:19:50.200
Indeed.

00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:53.890
The two of you
share this, all right ?

00:19:53.890 --> 00:19:57.040
After all, food is
the best souvenir.

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:03.560
Sister, you always treat us like 
gluttonous children, don't you ?

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:06.680
Yes...I want
to think so...

00:20:07.590 --> 00:20:08.660
Really...

00:20:20.730 --> 00:20:23.700
To the soldiers who took part in the last battle...

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:26.090
...His Excellency, our beloved and
respected National Defense Chairman...

00:20:26.090 --> 00:20:28.700
...will give words of
acknowledgement for services rendered.

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:30.690
What's that ?

00:20:30.690 --> 00:20:36.890
He probably wants to announce publicly, to those who really love their country...

00:20:36.890 --> 00:20:40.610
...and to all the soldiers who took part in the battle, his own control over the fleet.

00:20:40.610 --> 00:20:42.650
And I have to go to
a thing like that ?

00:20:42.650 --> 00:20:43.830
It can't be helped.

00:20:43.830 --> 00:20:49.200
Well, as always, think of this as part
of your salary, and accept it gracefully.

00:20:57.800 --> 00:21:01.640
Lady Annerose also
seems as well as ever...

00:21:01.640 --> 00:21:05.200
Who could be well,
imprisoned in a place like this ?!

00:21:06.640 --> 00:21:07.570
Lord Reinhard...

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:13.570
How many battles will it take
before I can rescue my sister...?

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:30.690
Good work, all of you.

00:21:31.660 --> 00:21:33.540
Here's Commodore Yang Wenli.

00:21:33.540 --> 00:21:36.810
I see.
You're the "Hero of El Facil ?"

00:21:39.790 --> 00:21:43.610
To you, what is the strategy
for certain victory ?

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:46.740
Well, for the sake of future
reference, I'd like to hear it.

00:21:46.740 --> 00:21:50.810
It is, first of all, to gather at least six times the number of the enemy...

00:21:50.810 --> 00:21:53.570
...distribute supplies
and equipment perfectly...

00:21:53.570 --> 00:21:56.680
...and convey the commander's
intentions without error.

00:21:58.690 --> 00:22:02.640
What we call the "outcome"
is decided off the battlefield.

00:22:02.640 --> 00:22:07.690
Tactics are nothing more than technically assisting the perfection of the strategy.

00:22:07.690 --> 00:22:09.890
That's rather simply put...

00:22:09.890 --> 00:22:14.620
...but doesn't the talent of the soldiers placed on the battlefield become a problem ?

00:22:15.450 --> 00:22:21.400
If the strategic plans are equally matched,
then of course, the soldiers' abilities are critical.

00:22:21.400 --> 00:22:26.740
But first of all, you can more or less make up for a discrepancy in quality with quantity.

00:22:26.740 --> 00:22:31.590
You don't think battles are
won by numbers, do you ?

00:22:31.590 --> 00:22:35.090
That kind of thinking is no
more than self justification...

00:22:35.090 --> 00:22:37.300
...by those who couldn't
find the numbers.

00:22:37.300 --> 00:22:40.680
It's unusual that a 
minority can beat a majority.

00:22:40.680 --> 00:22:44.630
If we'd started the war with that kind of miracle in hand from the outset...

00:22:44.630 --> 00:22:47.430
...there wouldn't be heaps of
people standing on the front lines.

00:22:49.760 --> 00:22:51.580
National Defense Chairman !

00:22:51.580 --> 00:22:54.430
Hey, Paeta.
Good work this time.

00:22:57.550 --> 00:23:00.710
I'm fed up with listening to
Truniht's big talk and derision.

00:23:01.710 --> 00:23:06.330
If he loves his country as much as he says,
why doesn't he go to the front lines himself ?

00:23:06.330 --> 00:23:07.440
Did you know ?

00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:10.620
While he was enlisted, although public
announcement of it has been prohibited...

00:23:10.620 --> 00:23:13.330
...he didn't take one
step off this planet.

00:23:13.330 --> 00:23:14.710
It's a standard story.

00:23:14.710 --> 00:23:18.890
People get more pro-war the 
farther they are from the front lines.

00:23:18.890 --> 00:23:22.900
I want to retire soon and live without
having to be polite to that kind of guy.

00:23:23.460 --> 00:23:26.490
You've started on that
topic again, I see.

00:23:26.490 --> 00:23:29.650
Whenever something disagreeable happens,
you start saying you'll retire.

00:23:29.650 --> 00:23:33.520
Even without any disagreeable
things, I want to retire.

00:23:33.520 --> 00:23:35.550
Without paying lip service ?

00:23:35.550 --> 00:23:41.340
Well, thinking formally for a while, there
probably won't be any big battles or invasions.

00:23:41.340 --> 00:23:42.850
Taking advantage of
this peaceful time...

00:23:42.850 --> 00:23:46.890
...I intend to work as much as
possible until my pension arrives.

00:24:05.550 --> 00:24:06.540
Kircheis  !

00:24:09.470 --> 00:24:10.540
Lord Reinhard.

00:24:10.540 --> 00:24:12.540
Kircheis !
It's a dispatch  !

00:24:12.540 --> 00:24:17.710
Early next year, leading a fleet of twenty
thousand ships, we'll invade Alliance territory.

00:24:19.590 --> 00:24:23.470
I can't believe I'll get an opportunity so
soon to get my hands on the Admiralty !

00:24:28.640 --> 00:24:34.500
Sister, aren't you happy that I'm succeeding
by rendering distinguished service ?

00:24:34.500 --> 00:24:36.900
That's impossible, isn't it ?

00:24:36.900 --> 00:24:38.990
Only, you see, Reinhard...

00:24:38.990 --> 00:24:43.540
...I think there's no need to be impatient about rendering too many distinguished services.

00:24:43.540 --> 00:24:46.440
I'm not impatient, Sister.

00:24:46.440 --> 00:24:50.620
But if there's an opportunity,
it's only natural to make the most of it.

00:24:50.620 --> 00:24:54.940
Reinhard, you're not
yet twenty years old...

00:24:54.940 --> 00:24:56.990
...and yet you're now
"His Excellency the Admiral."

00:24:56.990 --> 00:24:59.480
It's more than enough.

00:24:59.480 --> 00:25:01.540
I don't want you to
do anything unreasonable.

00:25:03.520 --> 00:25:05.530
Soon, I will be twenty.

00:25:05.530 --> 00:25:08.600
And thirty, and forty...

00:25:08.600 --> 00:25:13.530
If so, both my court rank and my official rank will probably become disproportionate.

00:25:13.530 --> 00:25:15.670
What will you do after that ?

00:25:20.300 --> 00:25:22.590
And what will
you do after that ?

00:25:22.590 --> 00:25:24.440
Wish for still more ?

00:25:28.100 --> 00:25:31.640
From the base of the mountain,
I've still only reached the middle.

00:25:31.640 --> 00:25:36.460
While I intend to climb, maybe
I'm really descending, maybe falling.

00:25:36.460 --> 00:25:39.330
There's nothing I can do
but think of the future.

00:25:40.900 --> 00:25:41.810
I see...

00:25:44.950 --> 00:25:47.400
Sieg, do me a favor.

00:25:47.400 --> 00:25:51.700
Please keep watch so that this mischievous boy doesn't stray from the road.

00:25:51.700 --> 00:25:55.680
Because if you let him go, he's a child who will go leaping who knows where.

00:25:55.680 --> 00:25:57.630
Yes, Lady Annerose.

00:25:58.450 --> 00:26:00.000
You're terrible, Sister  !

00:26:08.840 --> 00:26:10.730
What's the matter ?

00:26:10.730 --> 00:26:13.640
You told me not to
think of losing, right ?

00:26:14.450 --> 00:26:16.710
Lord Reinhard,
you're ill-natured.

00:26:18.780 --> 00:26:20.710
Lord Reinhard, this is...

00:26:23.700 --> 00:26:29.670
Certainly, as you say, if he
doesn't return, there's no problem.

00:26:30.350 --> 00:26:33.790
However, if by some miracle
he wins, what will you do ?

00:26:33.790 --> 00:26:37.640
Next is Fleet Admiral; later,
he might progress to Marquis.

00:26:37.640 --> 00:26:39.600
It's a matter of
if he wins, right ?

00:26:39.600 --> 00:26:41.440
The essential thing is
not allowing him to win.

00:26:41.440 --> 00:26:43.000
How ?

00:26:45.530 --> 00:26:50.670
Even if you say he has real talent,
he's also blessed with good staff officers.

00:26:50.670 --> 00:26:55.720
Certainly there are many problems
with Mittermeyer and Reuental...

00:26:55.720 --> 00:27:00.490
...who command both wings, but there is the criticism of diluting power.

00:27:00.490 --> 00:27:03.040
The fleet's Chief of Staff Officer,
Mecklinger, is the same type.

00:27:03.040 --> 00:27:08.560
In order to test his real talents, we
should make him fight without them, right ?

00:27:12.850 --> 00:27:15.730
Even the ship's captain
has been transferred ?!

00:27:15.730 --> 00:27:17.740
What in the world are
these personnel matters...?

00:27:17.740 --> 00:27:21.800
Essentially, they intend
to pluck off my limbs.

00:27:21.800 --> 00:27:23.740
At whose instigation,
I wonder...?

00:27:23.740 --> 00:27:25.780
You're not angry ?

00:27:25.780 --> 00:27:27.730
I'm angry !

00:27:27.730 --> 00:27:29.900
But I'm more
relieved than angry.

00:27:31.770 --> 00:27:34.530
Because you weren't
transferred, Kircheis.

00:27:35.650 --> 00:27:38.760
As long as you're with me,
there's nothing to fear.

00:27:39.400 --> 00:27:40.840
Lord Reinhard...

00:27:41.100 --> 00:27:42.770
How can I lose ?

00:27:42.770 --> 00:27:45.440
As long as you and
I fight together...

00:27:45.440 --> 00:27:47.800
Until we hold the
universe in our hands !

00:27:47.800 --> 00:27:49.550
Yes, Lord Reinhard.

00:27:57.400 --> 00:28:00.600
So who are the substitute
commanders this time ?

00:28:00.600 --> 00:28:02.430
Admiral Merkatz...

00:28:02.430 --> 00:28:03.800
...Vice Admiral Staaden...

00:28:03.800 --> 00:28:05.690
...Vice Admiral Erlache...

00:28:05.690 --> 00:28:06.820
...Rear Admiral Vogel...

00:28:06.820 --> 00:28:09.840
...and Rear Admiral Fahrenheit.
Those five people.

00:28:09.840 --> 00:28:12.240
With Merkatz, if you talk
about actual results...

00:28:12.240 --> 00:28:14.740
...it's strange that he hasn't
become a Fleet Admiral yet.

00:28:14.740 --> 00:28:17.870
He may not look like it, but he's steady, and he's good at using troops.

00:28:17.870 --> 00:28:21.440
However, being afflicted with
an unadaptable character...

00:28:21.440 --> 00:28:23.680
...he's a man who
advanced late in life.

00:28:23.680 --> 00:28:27.830
For a young commander, isn't he 
the hardest partner to use ?

00:28:27.830 --> 00:28:33.190
And concerning the existence of awkward people,
aren't the Fleet Admirals getting rid of some problems ?

00:28:33.190 --> 00:28:34.590
Yeah.

00:28:34.590 --> 00:28:36.650
I know Staaden well.

00:28:36.650 --> 00:28:40.600
When I was in Officers' School,
he was a lecturer in tactical theory.

00:28:40.600 --> 00:28:42.900
He couldn't turn to actual
battle from theory.

00:28:42.900 --> 00:28:46.840
We students called him
"Succumbed to Theory Staaden."

00:28:46.840 --> 00:28:50.680
For the time being, we can
say he's being evaluated ?

00:28:51.240 --> 00:28:57.650
Erlache and Fogel are the type that became admirals by combining a total number of 16 personnel matters.

00:28:57.650 --> 00:29:00.750
If they've become encumbrances,
they probably can't be saved.

00:29:01.450 --> 00:29:05.840
Rear Admiral Fahrenheit is
rumored to be another problem.

00:29:06.450 --> 00:29:08.890
Born a petty noble who became 
a soldier in order to eat...

00:29:08.890 --> 00:29:13.600
...he's a person who seems
to be full of flattery.

00:29:13.600 --> 00:29:19.640
He seems to have talent, but I've heard that he's inclined to rely on others to do his part.

00:29:19.640 --> 00:29:25.510
With this, on top of having his limbs cut off,
isn't he weighted down by chains ?

00:29:25.510 --> 00:29:29.670
No matter what you say, 
this time we can't do anything.

00:29:29.670 --> 00:29:31.570
Just believe in him.

00:29:34.670 --> 00:29:37.640
But the outcome of
a battle is a relative thing.

00:29:38.640 --> 00:29:41.560
Can't he also be saved by
the enemy's self-destruction ?

00:29:41.560 --> 00:29:43.520
That's true, but...

00:29:43.520 --> 00:29:46.590
Before that,
I have a good idea.

00:29:46.590 --> 00:29:52.510
Why don't we let that damned Phezzanni
Landsherr hear about this invasion plan...?

00:29:52.510 --> 00:29:55.940
Indeed !
Phezzan is the middleman.

00:29:55.940 --> 00:30:01.290
For the sake of trade, they might sell such information to the rebels' fleet.

00:30:01.290 --> 00:30:07.040
If so, it means they'll be able
to greet the brat fully prepared.

00:30:13.570 --> 00:30:17.300
What shall we do with this information, Your Excellency Landesherr ?

00:30:18.740 --> 00:30:22.290
In the most recent battle, the
 Empire was victorious, wasn't it ?

00:30:22.290 --> 00:30:23.290
Yes.

00:30:23.290 --> 00:30:28.290
Then to keep the balance, I'm afraid we must get the Free Planets Alliance to win this time.

00:30:28.290 --> 00:30:29.650
Understood.

00:30:29.650 --> 00:30:32.670
I'll allow this information to reach the ears of the Alliance government.

00:30:32.670 --> 00:30:34.290
Good.

00:30:40.040 --> 00:30:43.540
Leading big fleets,
a space fleet battle ?

00:30:43.540 --> 00:30:45.040
Political balance
and so forth...

00:30:45.040 --> 00:30:47.700
...with one informative investigation,
and those who groan about it...

00:30:49.440 --> 00:30:51.190
Such a troublesome matter.

00:30:54.290 --> 00:30:58.520
...which means, HQ Chief, please 
take a counterattack posture at once.

00:30:59.520 --> 00:31:00.630
Understood.

00:31:01.040 --> 00:31:04.380
They say the enemy
numbers 20,000 ships.

00:31:04.380 --> 00:31:09.770
Six times that is unreasonable, but if we send out twice the
amount, 40,000 ships in three fleets, it should be enough.

00:31:10.590 --> 00:31:12.190
Six times ?

00:31:12.190 --> 00:31:13.710
What does he mean ?

00:31:13.710 --> 00:31:16.700
It seems someone said
something uncalled for.

00:31:19.590 --> 00:31:26.840
He said to make the culprit who said that to the National Defense Chairman take responsibility.

00:31:26.840 --> 00:31:28.650
You're kidding !

00:31:28.650 --> 00:31:33.290
I...is the 2nd Fleet
really mobilizing, too ?

00:31:33.290 --> 00:31:35.040
What seems to be true
is that Admiral Paeta...

00:31:35.040 --> 00:31:38.710
...has vigorously requested a chance to recover his honor from the last time.

00:31:40.640 --> 00:31:46.500
In reality, the 2nd Fleet incurred the least damage in the previous battle.

00:31:46.500 --> 00:31:48.940
This time, because they're
calling it an easy victory...

00:31:48.940 --> 00:31:52.040
...including the commanders
of the 4th and 6th Fleets...

00:31:52.040 --> 00:31:56.710
...the National Defense Chairman was probably firm
in thinking he wants to make us distinguish ourselves.

00:31:57.710 --> 00:31:59.550
The 6th Fleet
is going, too ?

00:31:59.550 --> 00:32:01.500
Yeah.

00:32:01.500 --> 00:32:05.300
Oh, Lap is stationed in
the 6th Fleet, isn't he ?

00:32:05.900 --> 00:32:07.530
Yeah...

00:32:07.530 --> 00:32:09.710
Anyway, it'll be
within a few days.

00:32:09.710 --> 00:32:13.090
Just make your preparations
beforehand. Bye.

00:32:16.040 --> 00:32:17.390
Are you worried ?

00:32:18.290 --> 00:32:19.620
Yeah...

00:32:19.620 --> 00:32:22.290
I don't think Lap wants to 
go out to the front lines.

00:32:23.540 --> 00:32:24.560
I'm selfish.

00:32:25.090 --> 00:32:27.590
But they say it's an
easy victory this time.

00:32:27.590 --> 00:32:29.520
Rear Admiral Cazellnu, too.

00:32:29.520 --> 00:32:31.940
Even in a winning battle,
sacrifices result.

00:32:31.940 --> 00:32:35.690
You can't win by spilling
just one drop of allied blood.

00:32:35.690 --> 00:32:36.640
Usually...

00:32:36.640 --> 00:32:39.690
But Commodore,
if you aren't careful...

00:32:39.690 --> 00:32:41.600
Because it's not
a traffic accident.

00:32:41.600 --> 00:32:44.540
Even if they're told to be careful,
there are times when people die in battle.

00:32:44.540 --> 00:32:46.040
If that happens,
I'll be in a fix  !

00:32:46.040 --> 00:32:48.560
I'll go back to being
a war orphan again !

00:32:48.560 --> 00:32:52.530
I'm still only fourteen, but I'm planning on becoming a soldier in two years.

00:32:52.530 --> 00:32:55.090
Julian, do you intend
to become a soldier ?

00:32:55.090 --> 00:32:58.490
Yes.  My late father
was a soldier, too.

00:32:58.490 --> 00:33:00.690
More than anything,
I want to help you, Commodore !

00:33:01.570 --> 00:33:04.940
You don't particularly have to 
continue the work of your father.

00:33:04.940 --> 00:33:07.540
For example, my
father was a merchant.

00:33:07.540 --> 00:33:11.600
Besides, don't you
help me enough, Julian ?

00:33:11.600 --> 00:33:15.600
You're good at making this tea.
Your cooking is delicious, too.

00:33:15.600 --> 00:33:18.640
That's it.
Why don't you become a cook ?

00:33:18.640 --> 00:33:23.490
When I retire and go on a pension, I'll even give you a restaurant-opening ceremony.

00:33:23.490 --> 00:33:24.090
How about it ?

00:33:24.090 --> 00:33:26.380
Then you're opposed,
aren't you ?

00:33:26.380 --> 00:33:28.050
To me becoming a soldier.

00:33:31.840 --> 00:33:34.190
Do you want to be
a soldier that much ?

00:33:34.190 --> 00:33:35.190
Yes !

00:33:48.570 --> 00:33:54.390
I'm expecting great deeds
from{of} you, Reinhard von Musel.

00:33:54.390 --> 00:33:57.840
No, it's already
Count Lohengramm, isn't it ?

00:33:57.840 --> 00:34:01.680
I will make every effort
for your blessed words.

00:34:05.100 --> 00:34:08.300
If they aren't showier deeds beyond those you've already rendered...

00:34:08.300 --> 00:34:11.350
...I'm afraid the old courtiers,
who are apt to be noisy...

00:34:11.350 --> 00:34:16.860
...will also express discontent that you're
succeeding to the Lohengramm Countship.

00:34:16.860 --> 00:34:22.650
Their claim is that court rank and position are the results of great achievements.

00:34:23.740 --> 00:34:29.760
It isn't of great importance whether someone
succeeds to a countship or it becomes extinct, is it ?

00:34:29.760 --> 00:34:34.530
Although there are many who are 
convinced that they're important.

00:34:37.650 --> 00:34:43.540
How about this ?  I'm thinking that
I'd rather make you a Marquis...

00:34:44.240 --> 00:34:47.400
Marquis...was it ?

00:34:52.340 --> 00:34:58.400
While I am gratified by your words,
even a Countship is higher than I deserve.

00:34:58.400 --> 00:35:03.710
A Marquisate...In short, my being above the clouds, is not within my reach.

00:35:03.710 --> 00:35:05.550
So, you think so ?

00:35:05.550 --> 00:35:09.550
To say nothing of Marquis, even
Count is more than you deserve ?

00:35:09.550 --> 00:35:11.800
As you will,
Your Majesty.

00:35:11.800 --> 00:35:14.760
You think of yourself
as above the clouds ?

00:35:15.800 --> 00:35:22.900
It is said in the world "Kaiser" is more 
grand than "Marquis," but do you agree ?

00:35:23.640 --> 00:35:24.530
Yes.

00:35:25.720 --> 00:35:27.710
So, you agree, do you ?

00:35:27.710 --> 00:35:31.910
Well then, for the time being, you
should be diligent and aim for Count.

00:35:31.910 --> 00:35:37.090
And then after that,
aim for yet another thing.

00:35:54.760 --> 00:35:55.710
Lord Reinhard  !

00:36:04.650 --> 00:36:06.720
Kircheis, we're
going to the battlefield.

00:37:02.190 --> 00:37:04.730
I told you,
I'll be OK.

00:37:33.300 --> 00:37:37.190
Commodore, even at the front
lines, please take care to eat.

00:37:37.190 --> 00:37:40.400
Because, no matter how busy you are, it's no use if you don't eat punctually.

00:37:40.400 --> 00:37:43.100
It's OK. Because I
won't work that hard.

00:37:44.730 --> 00:37:46.300
Jean Robert...

00:37:52.770 --> 00:37:54.820
Please don't make
that kind of face.

00:37:54.820 --> 00:37:57.400
You shouldn't worry, this
time it's an easy victory.

00:37:57.400 --> 00:37:58.700
Right, Yang ?

00:37:58.700 --> 00:37:59.840
Y...yeah.

00:38:01.920 --> 00:38:04.200
At any rate,
take care...

00:38:04.200 --> 00:38:05.830
Come back in one
piece, all right ?

00:38:05.830 --> 00:38:07.650
Yeah, I promise.

00:38:07.650 --> 00:38:10.550
When I come back, let's go
look for a house together.

00:38:10.550 --> 00:38:11.860
A house where the
two of us can live.

00:38:11.860 --> 00:38:13.250
I promise.

00:38:24.770 --> 00:38:25.820
Oh, my lipstick

00:38:30.100 --> 00:38:32.730
Can I have this
as an amulet ?

00:38:34.190 --> 00:38:35.660
Yes, fine...

00:38:47.760 --> 00:38:48.710
Yang !

00:38:48.710 --> 00:38:49.750
Jean Robert !

00:38:50.750 --> 00:38:53.730
Please, both of you come
home in one piece, OK ?

00:38:53.730 --> 00:38:55.660
Yeah !

00:39:00.350 --> 00:39:03.190
What's the matter, Yang ?
Worried about something ?

00:39:03.190 --> 00:39:06.550
Even if you say twice the number of troops, if you make a mistake in moving them...

00:39:06.550 --> 00:39:07.860
It can't be an
easy victory ?

00:39:07.860 --> 00:39:08.830
Yeah.

00:39:08.830 --> 00:39:10.000
Hey, hey...

00:39:10.000 --> 00:39:11.990
If you're the Hero of
El Facil, it's unavoidable.

00:39:11.990 --> 00:39:13.700
It's OK, it's OK.

00:39:23.250 --> 00:39:25.670
At any rate, both of
us will come back alive.

00:39:26.740 --> 00:39:27.740
Yeah.

00:39:32.750 --> 00:39:33.750
See ya.

00:40:38.850 --> 00:40:40.800
The total number of 
enemy ships is 20,000.

00:40:40.800 --> 00:40:44.720
Our opposing fleet, in
three fleets, is 40,000 ships.

00:40:44.720 --> 00:40:47.360
In other words, twice
the enemy's strength.

00:40:47.950 --> 00:40:55.100
Each fleet will approach the enemy fleet from three
separate directions, forming a perfect envelopment.

00:40:55.100 --> 00:40:57.810
This is the same formation that our
fleet used against the Imperial Fleet...

00:40:57.810 --> 00:41:02.390
...in the historic Battle of Dagon
Starzone to gain perfect victory.

00:41:03.740 --> 00:41:06.950
As in that time, making
the most of the carnage...

00:41:06.950 --> 00:41:10.800
...by forcing the enemy into the siege net, we will then exterminate them.

00:41:10.800 --> 00:41:13.790
This time, too, our fleet's 
victory cannot be doubted !

00:41:16.810 --> 00:41:19.830
The predicted final battlefield
is the Astate Starzone !

00:41:38.150 --> 00:41:40.650
Are you looking at the
stars, Your Excellency ?

00:41:40.650 --> 00:41:41.680
Yes.

00:41:41.680 --> 00:41:42.450
The stars are good.

00:41:48.250 --> 00:41:53.550
In any age, in any society, when people are small, they look up at the stars...

00:41:53.550 --> 00:41:55.850
...and stretch out their
hands as if to grasp them.

00:41:55.850 --> 00:42:01.050
Then at last, they learn that their own arms aren't long enough to reach the stars.

00:42:01.050 --> 00:42:03.690
They call that
becoming an adult.

00:42:03.690 --> 00:42:06.690
But I don't think so.

00:42:06.690 --> 00:42:08.750
Without fail, those
stars will be in this hand !

00:42:17.770 --> 00:42:18.800
So...?

00:42:18.800 --> 00:42:23.810
As expected, the enemy is approaching from three sides with twice our strength.

00:42:23.810 --> 00:42:29.830
Concerning this, the five admirals have been
urgently requesting a meeting with Your Excellency.

00:42:30.150 --> 00:42:31.550
Really ?

00:42:31.550 --> 00:42:33.100
You won't see them ?

00:42:33.100 --> 00:42:34.500
No, I'll see them.

00:42:36.610 --> 00:42:39.700
Because they must've
already held council.

00:43:03.550 --> 00:43:08.350
Your Excellency, thank you very much for allowing us to voice our opinion.

00:43:09.350 --> 00:43:11.780
I already know what
you all want to say.

00:43:11.780 --> 00:43:13.840
That our fleet is in a
disadvantageous situation.

00:43:13.840 --> 00:43:17.700
You probably wanted to
call my attention to that.

00:43:17.700 --> 00:43:19.500
Exactly, Your Excellency.

00:43:20.290 --> 00:43:25.640
The enemy's 4th Fleet is positioned
to our front, numbering 12,000 ships.

00:43:25.640 --> 00:43:28.700
To our left, the enemy's
2nd Fleet, 15,000 ships.

00:43:28.700 --> 00:43:30.950
To our right, the
6th Fleet, 13,000 ships.

00:43:30.950 --> 00:43:34.650
If they combine, they are twice
our strength, at 40,000 ships.

00:43:34.650 --> 00:43:39.450
Our fleet is standing in an overwhelmingly disadvantageous situation.

00:43:39.450 --> 00:43:41.550
We shouldn't enter
into an exchange here...

00:43:41.550 --> 00:43:46.510
...but make an honorable retreat,
as long as we're at a disadvantage.

00:43:46.510 --> 00:43:48.710
We mustn't consider withdrawing.

00:43:48.710 --> 00:43:51.810
Why ?!  Will you let
us hear the reason ?

00:43:51.810 --> 00:43:55.950
Because we are in an overwhelmingly more advantageous situation than the enemy !

00:43:55.950 --> 00:43:57.780
What ?

00:43:59.810 --> 00:44:06.400
It seems you hold an opinion that's rather hard for a dense person like me to understand.

00:44:06.400 --> 00:44:10.850
I'd be grateful if you'd 
explain in a little more detail.

00:44:10.850 --> 00:44:13.770
You say the enemy
is twice our size.

00:44:13.770 --> 00:44:17.720
That, until the bitter end, is the 
story of adding up all the ships.

00:44:17.720 --> 00:44:22.850
The enemy, again making a wrong assumption, 
has dispersed its fleet strength in three directions.

00:44:22.850 --> 00:44:26.770
When you compare our concentrated fleet to any of those fleets, based on the numbers...

00:44:26.770 --> 00:44:30.740
...it's self-evident that our
side is at an advantage.

00:44:30.740 --> 00:44:34.840
Besides, because our fleet is placed in the center of the enemy trying to envelop us...

00:44:34.840 --> 00:44:39.600
...we can catch the enemy more quickly than the enemy can try to combine.

00:44:49.620 --> 00:44:56.610
In the end, our fleet is in a superior position to the enemy, both in concentration and mobility.

00:44:56.610 --> 00:44:59.760
What can this be called,
if not the conditions for victory ?!

00:45:00.850 --> 00:45:03.700
We're in no danger
of being enveloped.

00:45:03.700 --> 00:45:06.060
It's a chance to crush
the enemy one by one.

00:45:11.750 --> 00:45:15.500
He's going to try to use that kind of weak academic argument in actual battle ?!

00:45:17.770 --> 00:45:22.670
Your Excellency, what do you think
of the Fleet Commander's plan ?

00:45:32.750 --> 00:45:36.680
To be called a "weak academic argument" by "Succumbed to Theory Staaden ?"

00:45:36.680 --> 00:45:37.710
Then, after all...?

00:45:37.710 --> 00:45:40.500
Maybe the negative of
a negative is a positive.

00:45:40.500 --> 00:45:41.300
Yes, sir.

00:45:46.840 --> 00:45:49.850
The change in dispatch
will be fine.

00:45:49.850 --> 00:45:51.620
Isn't it interesting ?

00:45:56.760 --> 00:45:58.800
Your Excellency,
is it alright ?

00:45:58.800 --> 00:46:00.800
Everybody went back
in a bad mood.

00:46:01.720 --> 00:46:02.850
Let them go.

00:46:02.850 --> 00:46:06.730
Do they even have the spirit
to disobey a superior officer ?

00:46:06.730 --> 00:46:09.740
Grumbling all they want, and sick from worry that they'll lose a chance to be sarcastic.

00:46:09.740 --> 00:46:12.630
But maybe that's just
because they're introverted.

00:46:12.630 --> 00:46:17.800
Even if they don't rebel, by deciding on
sabotage, they may become a nuisance.

00:46:17.800 --> 00:46:21.890
You worry too much, as always.
Then, what should I do ?

00:46:21.890 --> 00:46:27.650
Among the five, Rear Admiral Fahrenheit
looked favorably on Your Excellency's plan.

00:46:27.650 --> 00:46:30.600
He's a person who originally
offered great promise.

00:46:30.600 --> 00:46:32.690
How about if we use
him in the vanguard ?

00:46:32.690 --> 00:46:34.750
Yes.  Please arrange
it at once.

00:46:34.750 --> 00:46:35.740
Yes, Your Excellency.

00:46:38.690 --> 00:46:42.400
Kircheis, when it's the two of us,
stop calling me "Your Excellency."

00:46:42.400 --> 00:46:43.450
I'm always telling
you that, aren't I ?

00:46:43.450 --> 00:46:45.700
I understand, but...

00:46:45.700 --> 00:46:47.000
If you understand,
then do it.

00:46:47.000 --> 00:46:51.200
Because when this battle's over,
you will also be called "Your Excellency."

00:46:52.420 --> 00:46:55.400
You'll be promoted to Commodore.
It'll be fun, won't it ?

00:47:00.810 --> 00:47:02.630
What's the matter, Kircheis ?

00:47:03.620 --> 00:47:06.630
No, it's nothing,
Lord Reinhard.

00:47:12.690 --> 00:47:15.890
I looked at the strategic
plan you presented.

00:47:15.890 --> 00:47:16.850
Yes ?

00:47:16.850 --> 00:47:19.400
It was a pretty
absorbing plan.

00:47:19.400 --> 00:47:22.880
However, even for a cautious plan,
isn't it rather conservative ?

00:47:23.550 --> 00:47:24.700
Do you think so ?

00:47:25.450 --> 00:47:29.700
As you yourself wrote, it certainly is a pretty hard-to-beat strategic plan.

00:47:29.700 --> 00:47:31.810
But there's no meaning
in just not losing.

00:47:31.810 --> 00:47:34.670
Our fleet surrounds the
enemy on three sides.

00:47:34.670 --> 00:47:36.690
Furthermore, it's a force
twice the enemy's.

00:47:36.690 --> 00:47:39.950
Based on this, why do we have to
have a plan so as "not to lose ?"

00:47:39.950 --> 00:47:43.810
But the envelopment
is not yet complete.

00:47:44.400 --> 00:47:46.840
At any rate, your
strategic plan is rejected.

00:47:55.680 --> 00:47:57.500
It goes without saying...

00:47:57.500 --> 00:47:59.790
...but it's not because
I bear you a grudge.

00:48:03.840 --> 00:48:05.810
It seems
you're bothered ?

00:48:06.950 --> 00:48:09.600
I have no idea
what he's thinking.

00:48:18.690 --> 00:48:19.810
How'd it go ?

00:48:20.880 --> 00:48:21.830
Oh, dear...

00:48:34.050 --> 00:48:40.800
We're asking for signatures to stop
cutting off funds from the fine arts !

00:48:41.550 --> 00:48:43.550
We're asking for
signatures to stop...

00:48:43.550 --> 00:48:44.550
Sign, please ?

00:48:45.100 --> 00:48:46.890
Please ?

00:48:49.950 --> 00:48:51.550
Signature, please...

00:48:51.550 --> 00:48:52.800
Professor Edwards ?!

00:48:52.800 --> 00:48:55.400
I'll help out, too.

00:49:00.850 --> 00:49:02.500
Thank you very much !

00:49:02.500 --> 00:49:04.800
Ma'am, is it true
you're getting married ?!

00:49:06.890 --> 00:49:07.790
Yes.

00:49:07.790 --> 00:49:09.000
Wow !
Congratulations !

00:49:09.000 --> 00:49:10.950
Congratulations !

00:49:10.950 --> 00:49:11.860
Thanks.

00:49:12.750 --> 00:49:13.950
Hang in there.

00:49:13.950 --> 00:49:17.850
Keep fighting for things
that aren't of use to the war.

00:49:17.850 --> 00:49:20.600
We absolutely
can't allow it !

00:49:20.600 --> 00:49:21.800
But...

00:49:21.800 --> 00:49:23.740
You can't give up !

00:49:23.740 --> 00:49:27.750
Even though it looks like this, when we were students, we did the same things.

00:49:27.750 --> 00:49:28.810
"We ?"

00:49:28.810 --> 00:49:34.100
Yes.  With the person I'm marrying,
and one other friend...

00:49:36.690 --> 00:49:40.770
Come back in one piece,
Jean Robert, Yang...

00:49:41.720 --> 00:49:42.840
Message from reconnaissance !

00:49:42.840 --> 00:49:45.770
The Imperial Fleet is not
at the expected coordinates !

00:49:45.770 --> 00:49:49.810
They're advancing rapidly,
and will contact the 4th Fleet !

00:49:49.810 --> 00:49:51.950
What ?!
That's absurd...

00:49:51.950 --> 00:49:53.400
It can't be !

00:50:07.400 --> 00:50:09.290
Imperial Fleet, rapidly approaching !

00:50:10.680 --> 00:50:12.730
What does this mean ?!

00:50:12.730 --> 00:50:14.700
What does the Imperial
Fleet have in mind ?

00:50:14.700 --> 00:50:17.400
What're they thinking ?
What a fix this is.

00:50:17.400 --> 00:50:19.530
The enemy commander knows
nothing of fleet movements.

00:50:19.530 --> 00:50:21.650
Is there a way of
fighting like this ?!

00:50:21.650 --> 00:50:23.300
Admiral, what'll you do ?

00:50:23.300 --> 00:50:28.400
Aren't you the staff officers who advocated
dividing up as a means of certain victory ?

00:50:28.400 --> 00:50:30.300
What's this
"what'll you do ?!"

00:50:31.300 --> 00:50:34.600
Urgent message to the
2nd and 6th Fleets !

00:50:34.600 --> 00:50:39.950
Tell them that we've engaged the enemy in space zone alpha 7.4, beta 3.9, gamma -0.6.

00:50:39.950 --> 00:50:41.700
We require
immediate assistance.

00:50:41.700 --> 00:50:43.400
It's no use !
They're jamming us !

00:50:44.710 --> 00:50:45.720
Admiral, the enemy...!

00:50:48.620 --> 00:50:50.400
All ships,
commence attack !

00:50:53.310 --> 00:50:55.500
Forward group,
counterattack !

00:50:55.500 --> 00:50:57.250
All ships, prepare
for all out battle !

00:51:11.950 --> 00:51:14.400
You damned incompetent,
you've reacted too late.

00:51:22.050 --> 00:51:24.400
Launch fighters.

00:51:24.400 --> 00:51:25.800
Switch to dogfight.

00:51:25.800 --> 00:51:27.810
Yes, sir !
Launch Valkyries !

00:51:28.550 --> 00:51:31.840
No matter whose distinguished service it becomes, we'll win, no matter what.

00:52:06.810 --> 00:52:08.500
Launch Spartanians !

00:52:21.760 --> 00:52:23.770
Blitzkrieg group,
to the front...

00:52:50.550 --> 00:52:52.200
Oh, shit !
Forward guns, fire !

00:53:04.740 --> 00:53:06.710
W...what're
they doing ?!

00:53:07.500 --> 00:53:08.740
What are they doing...?

00:53:09.740 --> 00:53:11.690
Come in, 4th Fleet !

00:53:11.690 --> 00:53:13.840
This is the 2nd Fleet
flagship, Patroklos !

00:53:13.840 --> 00:53:17.630
4th Fleet flagship,
Leonidas, come in !

00:53:17.630 --> 00:53:19.400
Come in, 4th Fleet !

00:53:19.400 --> 00:53:21.660
This is the 2nd Fleet
flagship, Patroklos !

00:53:21.660 --> 00:53:23.350
4th Fleet flagship, Leonidas !

00:53:23.350 --> 00:53:25.000
Come in !

00:53:32.700 --> 00:53:33.840
Commodore Yang !

00:53:33.840 --> 00:53:34.830
Sir !

00:53:34.830 --> 00:53:37.730
How do you view
this situation ?

00:53:37.730 --> 00:53:39.400
Give me your opinion.

00:53:39.400 --> 00:53:42.860
It means the enemy will
attack each fleet individually.

00:53:42.860 --> 00:53:47.750
It's a plan that depended on dealing 
with the 4th Fleet in front of it first of all.

00:53:47.750 --> 00:53:54.750
Since the 4th Fleet's the smallest, and the 6th and 2nd Fleets' distances apart are greater...

00:53:54.750 --> 00:53:57.650
...and if they time it well, even after 
they've dealt with the 4th Fleet...

00:53:57.650 --> 00:54:01.600
...they can attack either of us more
 quickly than we can combine.

00:54:01.600 --> 00:54:04.550
But the 4th Fleet, so easily...

00:54:04.550 --> 00:54:08.510
Both fleets clashed head on.

00:54:08.510 --> 00:54:12.650
Against the enemy's 20,000 ships,
the 4th Fleet has 12,000 ships.

00:54:12.650 --> 00:54:14.700
The outcome is
perfectly clear.

00:54:14.700 --> 00:54:19.800
If so, we must advance quickly to the battlefield and assist the 4th Fleet.

00:54:19.800 --> 00:54:23.400
If it goes well, it may even be possible
to destroy the Imperial Fleet.

00:54:23.400 --> 00:54:24.680
It's probably useless.

00:54:25.680 --> 00:54:26.800
What do you mean ?!

00:54:27.670 --> 00:54:31.690
By the time we arrive,
the battle will already be over.

00:54:31.690 --> 00:54:34.550
The enemy will leave
the battlefield...

00:54:34.550 --> 00:54:38.100
...and, more quickly than the 6th Fleet
and 2nd Fleet can combine...

00:54:38.100 --> 00:54:40.800
...will probably turn and
attack one of our flanks.

00:54:41.750 --> 00:54:43.450
So what are you
telling me to do ?!

00:54:44.450 --> 00:54:48.300
Combine the 2nd and 6th Fleets
using the shortest route...

00:54:48.300 --> 00:54:51.400
...and establish a new
battlefield in that space zone.

00:54:51.400 --> 00:54:54.000
If we combine both fleets,
becoming 28,000 strong...

00:54:54.000 --> 00:54:57.400
...we can have a more equally matched fight with an enemy of 20,000.

00:54:57.400 --> 00:55:00.770
So you're saying we leave
the 4th Fleet to its fate ?

00:55:00.770 --> 00:55:02.880
Even if we go right now,
we won't be in time.

00:55:03.250 --> 00:55:06.000
But we can't neglect
an allied fleet's crisis.

00:55:07.550 --> 00:55:08.650
Then, in the end...

00:55:08.650 --> 00:55:12.740
...each of our fleets will be lured into the enemy's individual attack strategy.

00:55:13.350 --> 00:55:14.800
It needn't
be that way.

00:55:14.800 --> 00:55:19.900
I'm sure the 4th Fleet won't be taken so easily.  If they can hold out...

00:55:20.150 --> 00:55:23.500
I told you a moment
ago, it's no use.

00:55:23.500 --> 00:55:28.670
Commodore Yang, reality doesn't come about just like the plan you spoke of.

00:55:28.670 --> 00:55:30.950
The enemy commander
is Count Lohengramm.

00:55:30.950 --> 00:55:32.750
He's young
and inexperienced.

00:55:32.750 --> 00:55:35.810
Compared to that, Vice Admiral Pastoll
is a veteran of 100 battles !

00:55:36.770 --> 00:55:40.950
But Count Lohengramm is the commander of the white ship in the previous battle.

00:55:40.950 --> 00:55:42.300
His style of command...

00:55:42.300 --> 00:55:43.500
Enough, Commodore !

00:56:15.000 --> 00:56:17.060
Organized resistance has ceased.

00:56:18.550 --> 00:56:20.830
Hereafter, it will become a matter of switching to a mop-up operation.

00:56:21.740 --> 00:56:22.810
There's no need.

00:56:23.250 --> 00:56:24.430
Sir ?

00:56:24.430 --> 00:56:26.780
The battle is
barely one third over.

00:56:27.660 --> 00:56:29.840
We should neglect such
things as straggling enemies.

00:56:29.840 --> 00:56:32.710
Rather than that, we should
prepare for the next fight.

00:56:32.710 --> 00:56:34.700
Understood, Your Excellency Commander-in-Chief.

00:56:36.760 --> 00:56:39.650
He's changed his
attitude a little, hasn't it ?

00:56:39.650 --> 00:56:41.810
Yes, it probably
couldn't help but change.

00:56:42.790 --> 00:56:47.300
Which fleet, the left or the right, do you think we should attack next, Kircheis ?

00:56:48.300 --> 00:56:52.670
It's possible to turn to either flank,
but your decision is made, right ?

00:56:52.670 --> 00:56:53.700
Well, yes.

00:56:53.700 --> 00:56:58.430
The 6th Fleet, which is positioned to the right, is smaller in size, isn't it ?

00:56:58.430 --> 00:56:59.700
Precisely.

00:56:59.700 --> 00:57:07.800
Advance as we are, changing course clockwise, attacking the 6th Fleet's right flank.

00:57:07.800 --> 00:57:09.700
About how much
time will it take ?

00:57:09.700 --> 00:57:11.500
About four hours.

00:57:11.500 --> 00:57:13.810
You've already
calculated it ?

00:57:13.810 --> 00:57:16.640
Transmit the order
to the whole fleet.

00:57:16.640 --> 00:57:17.630
Very good, Sir.

00:57:19.750 --> 00:57:21.860
Do you have
some objection ?

00:57:22.250 --> 00:57:24.400
No, I don't.

00:57:24.400 --> 00:57:29.860
As there is some spare time, I was thinking we should let the troops get some rest.

00:57:29.860 --> 00:57:32.730
Oh, yes.
I hadn't noticed.

00:57:32.730 --> 00:57:33.780
Have them
rest in shifts.

00:57:33.780 --> 00:57:34.720
Yes, sir.

00:57:39.700 --> 00:57:42.660
Doesn't our young
commander do pretty well ?

00:57:42.660 --> 00:57:44.620
What, didn't you know ?

00:57:44.620 --> 00:57:47.880
We've been saying for a long time 
that our admiral's luck is the best.

00:57:49.400 --> 00:57:54.760
We've just been stationed here, but we were 
previously under the command of a nobleman.

00:57:54.760 --> 00:57:56.950
When we came here,
because it was a noble again...

00:57:56.950 --> 00:58:00.670
...and because he was that kind of pretty boy, we thought he would be useless.

00:58:00.670 --> 00:58:02.850
But that's
your ignorance.

00:58:02.850 --> 00:58:04.600
You're right !

00:58:11.790 --> 00:58:13.650
They're a mere mob.

00:58:13.650 --> 00:58:16.720
In the end, victory and so forth,
is no more than fighting a mob !

00:58:16.720 --> 00:58:17.800
I think so, too !

00:58:17.800 --> 00:58:20.740
Anybody could beat
an enemy like that !

00:58:20.740 --> 00:58:23.730
Everything, regardless of that
kind of brat's effort or not !

00:58:23.730 --> 00:58:27.590
If it's going to be like this, can I stand to let only the brat have distinguished services ?

00:58:27.590 --> 00:58:29.450
Without fail, I'll use
it for my own ends.

00:58:41.860 --> 00:58:43.880
Is there no
helping the 4th Fleet ?

00:58:49.760 --> 00:58:53.690
When you fight, it can't be
helped that sacrifices will result.

00:58:53.690 --> 00:58:54.600
But...

00:58:54.600 --> 00:59:01.800
No, therefore, to get the best results,
the first sacrifices must be meaningful.

00:59:02.810 --> 00:59:09.850
When it comes to civil wars, it becomes
using soldiers effectively to make allies die ?

00:59:09.850 --> 00:59:13.150
Do you suppose our
commander understands that ?

00:59:13.720 --> 00:59:15.840
Because it's best
for the upper echelon ?

00:59:15.840 --> 00:59:18.500
But about this time,
the 6th Fleet...

00:59:23.760 --> 00:59:24.830
Jean Robert...

00:59:36.690 --> 00:59:39.780
So you're saying you have
an objection to this strategy ?

00:59:40.950 --> 00:59:44.770
There's no need to deliberately divide up twice the number of the enemy.

00:59:44.770 --> 00:59:48.800
Rather, concentrating our fleet strength, we have a better shot from the front.

00:59:48.800 --> 00:59:51.400
Based on the numbers,
isn't it better ?

00:59:51.400 --> 00:59:56.750
This strategy will repeat the annihilation of the Battle of the Dagon Starzone.

00:59:56.750 --> 00:59:58.950
Our Lt. Commander Lap, here...

00:59:58.950 --> 01:00:04.750
...is wiser than past commanders,
High Admirals Lin Pao and Yusuf Tparoul !

01:00:08.710 --> 01:00:09.690
Admiral.

01:00:11.660 --> 01:00:13.710
A message from the Vice
Commander in the rear group.

01:00:13.710 --> 01:00:15.700
Ship image seen at 4:30.

01:00:15.700 --> 01:00:16.860
Impossible to identify.

01:00:16.860 --> 01:00:18.720
4:30, is it ?!

01:00:18.720 --> 01:00:20.850
Y...yes, sir,
it's the 4:30 direction.

01:00:20.850 --> 01:00:23.630
We still can't determine
whether it's enemy or ally.

01:00:23.630 --> 01:00:26.830
Which 4:30 is it ?
A.M. or P.M. ?!

01:00:29.740 --> 01:00:30.810
Don't lose your heads.

01:00:30.810 --> 01:00:33.840
The enemy couldn't
be at 4:30, could it ?

01:00:33.840 --> 01:00:36.400
We're advancing rapidly
to the battlefield.

01:00:36.400 --> 01:00:38.800
After all, the enemy is in
the direction we're heading.

01:00:39.650 --> 01:00:40.860
But, Admiral...

01:00:40.860 --> 01:00:42.200
What ?!

01:00:43.500 --> 01:00:47.850
I believe the enemy has
moved the battlefield.

01:00:49.680 --> 01:00:51.730
Neglecting the 4th Fleet ?

01:00:51.730 --> 01:00:57.300
Sir, I'm speaking bluntly, but I believe the 4th Fleet is already defeated.

01:00:59.200 --> 01:01:02.750
That's a bold but unhappy estimation,
isn't it, Lieutenant Commander.

01:01:02.750 --> 01:01:05.630
It seems your mouth has
gotten loosened by grease.

01:01:16.670 --> 01:01:17.600
What's going on ?

01:01:18.650 --> 01:01:19.860
Enemy attack from
starboard rear !

01:01:21.400 --> 01:01:22.200
The enemy ?

01:01:22.200 --> 01:01:23.790
The enemy's behind us ?

01:01:23.790 --> 01:01:25.780
Could it be a
special enemy detachment ?

01:01:25.780 --> 01:01:29.750
Or else, could it truly mean the
4th Fleet is already broken ?

01:01:29.750 --> 01:01:31.660
Don't lose your heads !

01:01:31.660 --> 01:01:32.700
Counterattack !

01:01:32.700 --> 01:01:33.730
Open fire !

01:01:50.840 --> 01:01:55.800
Maybe the age of old soldiers
like us is already gone...

01:01:55.800 --> 01:01:58.790
Admiral, the enemy's ship
ranks are crumbling.

01:01:59.700 --> 01:02:03.300
Switch to short-range battle,
and break through the enemy formation.

01:02:10.650 --> 01:02:12.850
All ships, reverse course !

01:02:12.850 --> 01:02:14.060
Admiral !

01:02:14.060 --> 01:02:16.770
Even if we reverse course,
it'll only cause confusion !

01:02:16.770 --> 01:02:20.550
On the contrary, I think we
should advance at full speed...

01:02:20.550 --> 01:02:22.860
...and change course in the counterclockwise direction, to attack the enemy's back.

01:02:22.860 --> 01:02:26.840
Before we can reach the enemy's back, the vast majority of our allies will be defeated !

01:02:26.840 --> 01:02:28.700
A reverse-course
offensive it is !

01:02:28.700 --> 01:02:29.680
But...

01:02:29.680 --> 01:02:30.690
Shut up !

01:02:39.300 --> 01:02:40.620
Fools !

01:02:41.150 --> 01:02:42.100
Fire !

01:02:53.300 --> 01:02:55.810
Many small vessels
rapidly approaching this ship !

01:03:09.840 --> 01:03:10.780
It's a dogfight !

01:03:10.780 --> 01:03:12.610
Launch Spartanians !

01:03:31.950 --> 01:03:34.800
Isn't Merkatz also
doing pretty well ?

01:03:34.800 --> 01:03:38.690
He's a man who was piling up military experience
since before Your Excellency was born.

01:03:40.500 --> 01:03:43.810
There are many men whose long military experience is just napping and meals.

01:03:44.730 --> 01:03:47.680
The outcome will be
decided momentarily, but...

01:03:47.680 --> 01:03:49.640
Shall we give them
a chance to surrender ?

01:03:56.890 --> 01:03:58.860
You're kind,
aren't you, Kircheis ?

01:04:05.650 --> 01:04:06.950
Being attacked on all sides !

01:04:06.950 --> 01:04:08.400
Being attacked on all sides !

01:04:08.400 --> 01:04:09.640
Come in !

01:04:09.640 --> 01:04:10.600
The flagship's been hit !

01:04:10.600 --> 01:04:12.500
Reactor power
rapidly falling !

01:04:12.500 --> 01:04:14.500
What happened to
the P.A. system ?!

01:04:14.500 --> 01:04:15.760
They're rushing in !

01:04:15.760 --> 01:04:16.660
Come in...!

01:04:17.600 --> 01:04:18.600
Come in !

01:04:20.740 --> 01:04:21.710
Jessica...

01:04:23.410 --> 01:04:24.690
Commander, that's...!

01:04:25.810 --> 01:04:26.760
Here, too !

01:04:28.400 --> 01:04:29.730
We're completely surrounded !

01:04:37.600 --> 01:04:38.800
It's a luminous signal.

01:04:44.630 --> 01:04:45.720
Try and read it.

01:04:46.700 --> 01:04:47.800
Reading it...

01:04:47.800 --> 01:04:52.400
"Your ship is completely surrounded.
There is no path of escape."

01:04:52.400 --> 01:04:56.300
"Surrender. We promise
lenient treatment..."

01:05:01.300 --> 01:05:02.800
Surrender, is it...?

01:05:03.250 --> 01:05:04.800
They can't be serious !

01:05:04.800 --> 01:05:07.720
Are they telling me to
accept the shame of living ?!

01:05:08.500 --> 01:05:11.500
But, Admiral, even smeared
with temporary disgrace...

01:05:11.500 --> 01:05:13.750
...if we live, there will be
a chance to fight again.

01:05:13.750 --> 01:05:14.750
Here...

01:05:15.600 --> 01:05:17.700
Damn you...!
Do you begrudge your life ?

01:05:17.700 --> 01:05:19.950
Except for praying for God's help, there is
nothing to do but die in an honorable defeat !

01:05:19.950 --> 01:05:22.860
By charging, I'll show the
enemy proof I'm a soldier...!

01:05:22.860 --> 01:05:24.600
That's a meaningless death !

01:05:24.600 --> 01:05:25.740
Shut up, coward !

01:05:26.810 --> 01:05:28.950
Just for the sake
of self-satisfaction...

01:05:28.950 --> 01:05:31.770
...you're trying to take a lot
of soldiers along with you !

01:05:31.770 --> 01:05:32.800
Which is more cowardly ?!

01:05:33.700 --> 01:05:35.400
Are you rebelling ?!

01:05:35.400 --> 01:05:36.800
Arrest Lieutenant Commander Lap !

01:05:36.800 --> 01:05:38.670
For the crime of mutiny !

01:05:39.680 --> 01:05:39.880
Stop it !

01:05:39.880 --> 01:05:41.800
Everyone, do you want
to die for nothing ?!

01:05:41.800 --> 01:05:44.670
Don't be poisoned together just
to satisfy a pathetic soldier !

01:05:48.700 --> 01:05:50.200
All ahead full !

01:06:34.400 --> 01:06:35.800
Jessica...

01:06:50.710 --> 01:06:52.400
Jessica...

01:06:52.400 --> 01:06:54.810
When I come back,
we'll marry...

01:06:54.810 --> 01:06:56.500
I'll come back...

01:06:56.500 --> 01:06:57.710
For sure...

01:07:37.400 --> 01:07:38.900
Jean Robert...

01:07:45.450 --> 01:07:47.840
So the 6th Fleet, too ?

01:07:47.840 --> 01:07:50.300
Yeah. Probably.
By now...

01:07:50.960 --> 01:07:52.770
What a waste !

01:07:52.770 --> 01:07:53.950
Then, Lap...?

01:07:53.950 --> 01:07:55.880
I don't know that.

01:07:55.880 --> 01:07:58.960
Even if you say "wiped out," it can't be that not a single ship will come back.

01:07:58.960 --> 01:08:00.900
All we can do is pray ?

01:08:02.980 --> 01:08:09.110
But what we must now do is avoid a reappearance of mistakes and control the mounting casualties.

01:08:09.110 --> 01:08:10.190
What will you do ?

01:08:10.190 --> 01:08:11.830
There's a measure I can take.

01:08:11.830 --> 01:08:14.000
But will I be given the chance
to make the most of it...?

01:08:15.180 --> 01:08:17.030
What a shame.

01:08:17.030 --> 01:08:19.250
Though, if you had
more authority, Yang...

01:08:19.250 --> 01:08:21.950
...we would've managed without
producing so many sacrifices.

01:08:21.950 --> 01:08:24.700
Soldiers have a duty
to follow orders.

01:08:24.700 --> 01:08:28.100
Exceeding that, and acting
forcibly, can't be forgiven.

01:08:28.100 --> 01:08:29.900
If I did that
kind of thing...

01:08:29.900 --> 01:08:33.020
...at the least, we would end up not being the fleet of a democratic nation.

01:08:33.700 --> 01:08:37.110
Both the 4th and 6th Fleets
have probably been wiped out.

01:08:37.110 --> 01:08:41.000
Only our fleet is operational, but aren't we fewer in number than the enemy ?

01:08:41.000 --> 01:08:42.110
I want some information.

01:08:42.110 --> 01:08:45.070
What's going on,
the present situation...

01:08:45.070 --> 01:08:47.020
We didn't plan for this.

01:08:47.020 --> 01:08:51.700
Weren't we supposed to envelop the enemy
from three sides and wipe them out ?

01:08:51.700 --> 01:08:53.900
What does the Commander
intend to do...?

01:09:05.990 --> 01:09:07.000
Enemy fleet approaching !

01:09:07.000 --> 01:09:08.130
In the midst of a
high speed approach !

01:09:09.040 --> 01:09:11.100
The direction will be
between 1 and 2 o'clock.

01:09:11.100 --> 01:09:14.070
The direction is 1:20,
eleven degree angle of inclination !

01:09:16.700 --> 01:09:18.050
Prepare for battle !

01:09:19.010 --> 01:09:19.940
Too late.

01:09:25.500 --> 01:09:27.110
Open all gun ports, attack...!

01:10:00.090 --> 01:10:01.020
Commander !

01:10:08.030 --> 01:10:08.990
Fleet Commander Paeta !

01:10:12.150 --> 01:10:14.140
Fleet Commander Paeta
has been wounded.

01:10:14.140 --> 01:10:17.140
Please send a doctor and
nurse to the bridge.

01:10:17.140 --> 01:10:20.080
Engineering, immediately investigate and repair the damage to the ship's hull.

01:10:20.080 --> 01:10:22.110
The reports can wait
until after that.

01:10:22.110 --> 01:10:24.950
Are there any
unhurt officers ?

01:10:24.950 --> 01:10:26.050
I'm OK.

01:10:34.180 --> 01:10:36.000
No others...?

01:10:43.800 --> 01:10:45.600
We've headed them
off, haven't we.

01:10:45.600 --> 01:10:48.000
With this,
it's a perfect victory.

01:10:48.000 --> 01:10:50.010
Our enemy is the
Alliance 2nd Fleet.

01:10:51.850 --> 01:10:53.500
In the 2nd Fleet,
certainly...

01:10:55.090 --> 01:10:56.500
That man is there.

01:10:57.600 --> 01:10:59.930
Commodore Yang Wenli.

01:11:05.000 --> 01:11:08.010
Six ribs are broken.
We'll treat him at once.

01:11:10.040 --> 01:11:11.920
Commodore Yang...

01:11:14.750 --> 01:11:17.930
You take command
of the fleet...

01:11:17.930 --> 01:11:19.810
Me ?

01:11:19.810 --> 01:11:25.000
At any rate, you're the highest
ranking among the uninjured officers.

01:11:25.830 --> 01:11:29.820
Prove your skill as
an expert tactician...

01:11:30.780 --> 01:11:31.780
Commander !

01:11:33.780 --> 01:11:35.850
No, he just passed out.

01:11:35.850 --> 01:11:37.250
Bring a stretcher, quickly !

01:11:41.880 --> 01:11:43.750
Gently, gently now...

01:11:45.650 --> 01:11:46.930
You're being appraised, eh ?

01:11:54.900 --> 01:11:56.700
Announcing to
the whole fleet...

01:11:56.700 --> 01:12:00.250
I am Commander-in-Chief Paeta's next ranking staff officer, Commodore Yang.

01:12:00.250 --> 01:12:02.100
The flagship
Patroklos is damaged...

01:12:02.100 --> 01:12:03.920
...the Commander-in-Chief
is also badly hurt.

01:12:03.920 --> 01:12:07.830
By the Commander's orders, 
I am taking over command of the fleet.

01:12:11.750 --> 01:12:13.150
Your Excellency,
it's an enemy broadcast.

01:12:13.870 --> 01:12:16.890
Don't worry. If you follow
my orders, we'll be saved.

01:12:16.890 --> 01:12:20.010
Those who want to return alive, I'd like you to be calm and follow my instructions.

01:12:20.010 --> 01:12:25.950
We're losing at present, but the essential thing is that we should win at the last moment.

01:12:26.840 --> 01:12:28.950
Even I'm talking big,
aren't I...?

01:12:28.950 --> 01:12:30.830
No, we expect it.

01:12:31.450 --> 01:12:32.880
We won't lose.

01:12:32.880 --> 01:12:36.960
Until I issue new orders, each ship is
to concentrate on individual bombardment.

01:12:41.810 --> 01:12:42.880
He came out, after all.

01:12:44.870 --> 01:12:46.950
"We won't lose...?"

01:12:47.650 --> 01:12:50.840
Considering the situation, how
does he intend to reverse it ?

01:12:51.760 --> 01:12:54.750
Well, fine. Shall we go to 
view the performance ?

01:12:55.800 --> 01:12:56.570
Kircheis ?

01:12:56.570 --> 01:12:57.870
Yes, sir ?

01:12:57.870 --> 01:12:59.750
Rearrange the
battle lines.

01:12:59.750 --> 01:13:03.800
Notify the whole fleet to
take a spindle formation.

01:13:03.800 --> 01:13:04.950
You know why,
don't you ?

01:13:04.950 --> 01:13:08.200
Do you intend to break
through the center ?

01:13:08.200 --> 01:13:09.950
Yes. Just as
I expected of you.

01:13:39.780 --> 01:13:41.980
The enemy is taking
a spindle formation.

01:13:41.980 --> 01:13:44.830
As I thought. They're going to 
try to break through the center.

01:13:45.790 --> 01:13:47.600
Break through
the center ?

01:13:47.600 --> 01:13:51.040
The morale that destroyed the
4th and 6th Fleets is high.

01:13:51.040 --> 01:13:53.900
It's probably a natural tactic
for the Imperial Fleet.

01:13:53.900 --> 01:13:55.820
How do you intend
to cope with it ?

01:13:55.820 --> 01:13:56.960
I'm thinking of
a countermeasure.

01:13:57.940 --> 01:14:00.040
However, how will we
communicate it to our allies ?

01:14:00.040 --> 01:14:02.850
There is the danger that the enemy will intercept our communications.

01:14:02.850 --> 01:14:03.980
Don't worry.

01:14:03.980 --> 01:14:09.100
Using multiple comms circuits we should just transmit 
"open the C-4 circuits of the ship's strategic computer."

01:14:09.100 --> 01:14:12.850
If it's just that, even if the enemy
intercepts it, they probably can't decipher it.

01:14:12.850 --> 01:14:15.850
So, predicting that the
situation would be like this...

01:14:15.850 --> 01:14:18.810
...you input all the strategic
information into the computers ?

01:14:18.810 --> 01:14:21.350
Yeah.  Although it would've been
better not to have had to use it.

01:14:23.790 --> 01:14:26.840
Never mind that, please
transmit the order quickly.

01:14:26.840 --> 01:14:27.850
Yes, at once.

01:14:29.700 --> 01:14:31.250
With this, when
it can't go well...

01:14:33.030 --> 01:14:35.250
I'll cook something up
while scratching my head.

01:14:50.910 --> 01:14:52.790
All ships - Charge !

01:14:56.450 --> 01:14:57.450
Charge !

01:15:00.910 --> 01:15:02.100
Charge !

01:15:19.350 --> 01:15:20.750
Enemy ship approaching !

01:15:22.000 --> 01:15:23.980
Judging from the ship type, it appears to be the battleship Wallenstein!

01:15:26.350 --> 01:15:27.830
Main guns -
Even firing !

01:15:38.770 --> 01:15:39.950
Another battleship,
the Krunten !

01:15:39.950 --> 01:15:40.980
Keep firing !

01:15:47.880 --> 01:15:49.250
Rotate !

01:16:20.830 --> 01:16:22.920
The enemy's morale
is high, isn't it.

01:16:22.920 --> 01:16:27.200
We might be watching the moment
of birth of a famous commander.

01:16:28.200 --> 01:16:29.820
Famous commander ?

01:16:30.820 --> 01:16:34.750
They call "famous commanders" those who can make their subordinates embrace the faith that they won't be defeated.

01:16:35.810 --> 01:16:41.350
Isn't the height of the enemy's morale proof that Count
Lohengramm can get his hands on and support that faith ?

01:16:53.850 --> 01:16:55.750
At any rate,
we've won, haven't we.

01:16:58.780 --> 01:17:00.830
At any rate,
it seems to be going well.

01:17:21.550 --> 01:17:22.770
Dammit...!

01:17:23.800 --> 01:17:24.750
Now !

01:17:24.750 --> 01:17:25.820
Engines, full thrust !

01:17:33.450 --> 01:17:34.750
The enemy has divided
to the left and right !

01:17:34.750 --> 01:17:37.500
They're advancing at high speed
along both our flanks !

01:17:39.150 --> 01:17:40.150
Kircheis !

01:17:42.920 --> 01:17:44.950
We've been outwitted...

01:17:44.950 --> 01:17:47.920
The enemy, divided into two sides,
intending to turn to our fleet's rear.

01:17:48.830 --> 01:17:51.780
They've turned our central 
breakthrough tactic back against us...!

01:17:53.870 --> 01:17:55.500
What will you do ?

01:17:55.500 --> 01:17:57.820
Reverse course and
counterattack ?

01:18:00.030 --> 01:18:01.930
Stop joking.

01:18:01.930 --> 01:18:06.960
Are you telling me to be more of an imbecile
than the commander of the enemy's 4th Fleet?

01:18:06.960 --> 01:18:09.010
Then we can only advance.

01:18:09.450 --> 01:18:10.350
Exactly.

01:18:11.950 --> 01:18:14.790
Fleet, full speed ahead !

01:18:24.810 --> 01:18:26.450
We did it !
We've taken their back !

01:18:26.450 --> 01:18:27.750
No, not yet.

01:18:27.750 --> 01:18:31.450
Keep advancing like this, clockwise,
sticking to the enemy's back.

01:18:31.450 --> 01:18:32.100
Hurry !

01:18:33.990 --> 01:18:36.030
Advance ?!
That idiot !

01:18:36.030 --> 01:18:37.810
The enemy's behind us !

01:18:37.810 --> 01:18:39.850
Reverse course !
Rapid reverse course !

01:18:53.000 --> 01:18:55.150
The battleship Heilenheim
has been destroyed !

01:18:55.150 --> 01:18:56.840
Rear Admiral Erlache
died in battle !

01:18:57.820 --> 01:18:59.920
Was he so
shortsighted ?!

01:18:59.920 --> 01:19:01.010
He got what
he deserved.

01:19:38.350 --> 01:19:40.840
This is the first time I've
ever seen a formation like this.

01:19:40.840 --> 01:19:41.880
Probably so.

01:19:48.940 --> 01:19:50.920
What an awkward formation !

01:19:51.900 --> 01:19:54.350
With this, isn't it a
battle of attrition...?

01:19:58.010 --> 01:20:00.560
Because this, too,
is a battle of attrition.

01:20:00.560 --> 01:20:02.900
If we continue like this,
neither side can win.

01:20:02.900 --> 01:20:05.750
If the enemy notices that
, they'll soon begin to withdraw.

01:20:09.040 --> 01:20:10.960
Kircheis, what
do you think ?

01:20:10.960 --> 01:20:14.780
Shouldn't there be
a chance soon...?

01:20:14.780 --> 01:20:15.960
You think so, too ?

01:20:16.550 --> 01:20:20.980
Even if we continue to fight,
the damage to both sides will just increase.

01:20:20.980 --> 01:20:23.350
Strategically,
it's meaningless.

01:20:25.880 --> 01:20:28.000
Do you think
it's humiliating ?

01:20:28.920 --> 01:20:32.860
It's not that, but...
I wanted to win a little more.

01:20:32.860 --> 01:20:35.150
While surrounded by an enemy
twice our size on three sides...

01:20:35.150 --> 01:20:36.550
...you destroyed two fleets with
the tactic of individual attack...

01:20:36.550 --> 01:20:40.910
...and while turned back upon by the
last enemy, you fought well-matched.

01:20:40.910 --> 01:20:43.100
Isn't it enough ?

01:20:43.100 --> 01:20:47.000
To hope for more
is rather greedy.

01:20:47.000 --> 01:20:51.000
I know. There'll also be more 
excitement at some future date.

01:21:02.960 --> 01:21:05.100
Yang Wenli...

01:21:05.100 --> 01:21:07.350
He fights well,
doesn't he ?

01:21:09.450 --> 01:21:13.850
Kircheis, send a message
to Yang Wenli in my name.

01:21:14.810 --> 01:21:16.780
What shall I say...?

01:21:23.150 --> 01:21:24.040
A message ?

01:21:25.080 --> 01:21:29.970
"Expressing respect for your brave fight; your health until the day we fight again."

01:21:29.970 --> 01:21:34.000
"Imperial Fleet High
Admiral von Lohengramm."

01:21:34.000 --> 01:21:35.040
That's all.

01:21:35.970 --> 01:21:37.010
Oh, dear...

01:21:37.010 --> 01:21:39.960
He means, "The next time we 
meet, I'll smash you to bits."

01:21:39.960 --> 01:21:41.910
What shall I do ?
Send an answer ?

01:21:41.910 --> 01:21:43.150
No, leave it.

01:21:43.150 --> 01:21:45.700
Because the other side isn't
expecting a thing like that.

01:21:46.800 --> 01:21:49.250
Rather than that, find every
survivor from the other fleets.

01:21:49.250 --> 01:21:51.900
I want to save as
many as possible.

01:21:51.900 --> 01:21:52.700
Roger !

01:21:54.070 --> 01:21:55.180
Oh, after that...

01:21:56.960 --> 01:21:57.750
Jean...

01:21:57.750 --> 01:22:01.070
I mean, please look into the
situation of the 6th Fleet.

01:22:02.800 --> 01:22:03.800
Roger !

01:22:17.150 --> 01:22:20.030
If I had a little
more authority...?

01:22:25.590 --> 01:22:29.920
Return to the Imperial Capital !
Fleet - order ship ranks !

01:22:54.750 --> 01:22:57.600
We've seen
intriguing magic.

01:22:57.600 --> 01:22:59.800
Count Lohengramm
and Yang Wenli...

01:22:59.800 --> 01:23:01.030
Interesting.

01:23:01.030 --> 01:23:06.150
Tell each of our High Commissioners' Offices to gather data on them as soon as possible.

01:23:06.150 --> 01:23:06.700
Yes, sir.

01:25:01.070 --> 01:25:02.930
Jean Robert...

01:25:03.970 --> 01:25:05.050
You...

01:25:05.050 --> 01:25:06.050
For what...?

01:25:25.000 --> 01:25:29.740
LEGEND OF THE GALACTIC HEROES

01:25:25.000 --> 01:25:29.740
Overture to a New Battle

01:26:38.080 --> 01:26:43.600
I'm appointing you Commander
of the newly formed 13th Fleet.

01:26:44.960 --> 01:26:46.500
Its first duty...

01:26:47.850 --> 01:26:49.970
...is to capture
Iserlohn Fortress.

01:26:53.900 --> 01:26:55.130
I'll do what I can.

01:27:32.400 --> 01:27:38.400
Yang Wenli:

01:27:32.400 --> 01:27:38.400
Tomiyama Kei

01:27:38.400 --> 01:27:44.400
Mittermeyer:

01:27:38.400 --> 01:27:44.400
Mori Katsuji

01:27:44.400 --> 01:27:50.400
Truniht:

01:27:44.400 --> 01:27:50.400
Ishizuka Unshou

01:28:08.400 --> 01:28:15.400
Translation:
Sue Shambaugh

01:28:15.400 --> 01:28:24.400
Time Editing:
Central Anime(Kansas)

01:28:24.400 --> 01:28:32.400
Additional Editing:
Central Anime(Kansas)
